WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.670
An equity goal describes a change worth working toward.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.210
The practical question is how the work in front

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:09.110
of us could contribute to that change. A course,

4
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.170
a tool, or a team conversation can help, but

5
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.450
its value depends on what people are able to

6
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:18.150
do with it afterward. Connecting Equity Goals, Learning, and

7
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.150
Everyday Practice introduces a simple way to explain that

8
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:21.770
relationship.

9
00:00:23.051 --> 00:00:25.831
You will use a logic model: a description of

10
00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:28.991
the knowledge and resources available, the work people do,

11
00:00:29.151 --> 00:00:31.451
what that work produces, and the change it is

12
00:00:31.471 --> 00:00:34.451
intended to support. The model is useful because it

13
00:00:34.471 --> 00:00:37.491
makes the connection open to discussion. It does not

14
00:00:37.511 --> 00:00:41.311
make the intended result happen automatically. In the service

15
00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:44.191
example, staff knowledge and community accounts inform a review

16
00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.171
of a service-change notice. The review produces a clearer

17
00:00:47.191 --> 00:00:47.591
draft.

18
00:00:48.064 --> 00:00:51.124
The intended result is that readers can understand and

19
00:00:51.144 --> 00:00:53.784
use the next step. Those are connected, but they

20
00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:56.844
are different. A clear draft may still need review,

21
00:00:56.944 --> 00:00:59.224
release, a usable way to reach people, and a

22
00:00:59.244 --> 00:01:02.204
working response route. If any of those conditions fails,

23
00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:05.164
the intended benefit may not reach the reader. The

24
00:01:05.184 --> 00:01:07.964
course connects this reasoning with the Aging and Disability

25
00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:11.124
Services Administration's six equity goal areas.

26
00:01:11.744 --> 00:01:16.224
They concern eliminating disparities, community engagement, hiring and retention,

27
00:01:16.544 --> 00:01:20.184
learning and development, contracts and procurement, and communication and

28
00:01:20.204 --> 00:01:23.344
accessibility. The goals relate to one another. A service

29
00:01:23.364 --> 00:01:26.764
communication may benefit from staff learning and community participation

30
00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:30.024
as well as clearer wording. A workforce opportunity may

31
00:01:30.044 --> 00:01:33.304
involve recruitment, development, and attention to disparities at the

32
00:01:33.324 --> 00:01:35.944
same time. DSD can choose approaches that fit its

33
00:01:35.964 --> 00:01:38.224
work while remaining aligned with the plan and relevant

34
00:01:38.244 --> 00:01:38.784
requirements.

35
00:01:39.554 --> 00:01:42.214
You do not need to force every activity under

36
00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:45.354
every goal. Nor should a useful equity question disappear

37
00:01:45.374 --> 00:01:47.834
because it does not fit neatly beneath one heading.

38
00:01:48.354 --> 00:01:50.834
The starting point is the actual concern and the

39
00:01:50.854 --> 00:01:53.514
change the team can help bring about. The workplace

40
00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:57.534
example considers a clearer development invitation. Learning and employee

41
00:01:57.554 --> 00:02:00.634
perspectives inform a review, and the team produces a

42
00:02:00.654 --> 00:02:03.814
better invitation. That does not guarantee that people can

43
00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:04.334
take part.

44
00:02:04.872 --> 00:02:08.472
Scheduling, preparation, workload, and the learning arrangement may still

45
00:02:08.492 --> 00:02:11.572
matter. A logic model helps a supervisor see those

46
00:02:11.592 --> 00:02:14.432
conditions instead of treating the completed communication as the

47
00:02:14.452 --> 00:02:17.812
entire result. Community knowledge also helps define what a

48
00:02:17.832 --> 00:02:20.752
useful result means. In the course, a participant says

49
00:02:20.772 --> 00:02:23.252
the service notice still leaves the response route unclear.

50
00:02:23.732 --> 00:02:26.332
If staff have defined success only as fewer questions,

51
00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:27.432
they may miss the concern.

52
00:02:27.962 --> 00:02:31.402
The more useful inquiry is whether people understand the

53
00:02:31.422 --> 00:02:34.162
next step and can use it. Their experience may

54
00:02:34.182 --> 00:02:36.822
change the outcome the team should pay attention to.

55
00:02:37.242 --> 00:02:39.502
By the end, you will write one clear connection

56
00:02:39.522 --> 00:02:42.842
between a goal, a relevant learning or work activity,

57
00:02:43.022 --> 00:02:45.662
and a change you hope to support. You will

58
00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:48.822
identify the assumptions that need checking and the responsibilities

59
00:02:48.842 --> 00:02:49.562
involved.

60
00:02:50.143 --> 00:02:53.483
The purpose is a practical explanation colleagues can use

61
00:02:53.503 --> 00:02:56.923
together: why this work matters, what it contributes, and

62
00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.523
what would help you understand whether that contribution is

63
00:02:59.543 --> 00:03:02.563
making a difference. Consider a reader who receives the

64
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:05.203
revised notice but still cannot find the next step.

65
00:03:05.663 --> 00:03:09.343
The notice exists; the intended benefit is uncertain. In

66
00:03:09.363 --> 00:03:12.043
your model, connect staff learning with the wording change,

67
00:03:12.123 --> 00:03:14.283
then ask what the reader can understand and do.

68
00:03:14.777 --> 00:03:18.177
If the contact route is unusable, another wording edit

69
00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:20.557
may not solve the problem. This is how the

70
00:03:20.577 --> 00:03:23.757
model helps you choose where attention belongs, while keeping

71
00:03:23.777 --> 00:03:25.257
the reader’s experience central.
